    "type": "message",
    "user": "U06M6E5J2SC",
    "text": "1,2: No, why?\nDuring a `pwrite(*buf, size, offset)` syscall, `size` bytes from `buf` is written to the file as if you did `lseek(offset)`  for just that write. That's the `ctx.size` and `ctx.offset` in the `compress_ctx`.\nbpf_copy_from_buffer use the same names, but they mean something else.\n`int bpf_copy_from_buffer(void *ctx, unsigned long copy_offset, void *dest, unsigned long copy_size)` should work like `memcpy(dest, buf+copy_offset, copy_size)`but checking for validity of the access: returning an error when ``copy_offset\u003esize``  and copying less otherwise.\n\n3. These fields are there for completeness of information about the syscall.",
    "ts": "1744900623.314309",
    "thread_ts": "1744900623.314309",
